{"name":"Online Lime","hex":"#468c3e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"online","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a system: connected (generally electrically) to a larger network.\nOf a generator or power plant: connected to the grid.\nOf a computer: actively connected to the Internet or to some other communications service.","Of a generator or power plant: connected to the grid."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["While online; while in a running or active state, or connected to the Internet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/online"},{"term":"lime","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any inorganic material containing calcium, usually calcium oxide (quicklime) or calcium hydroxide (slaked lime).","Any gluey or adhesive substance that traps or captures; sometimes a synonym for birdlime."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To treat with calcium hydroxide or calcium oxide (lime).","To smear with birdlime.\n To ensnare, catch, entrap."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lime"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lime (material)","blocks":[{"text":"Lime is an inorganic material composed primarily of calcium oxides and hydroxides. It is also the name for calcium oxide which is used as an industrial mineral and is made by heating calcium carbonate in a kiln. Calcium oxide can occur as a product of coal-seam fires and in altered limestone xenoliths in volcanic ejecta. The International Mineralogical Association recognizes lime as a mineral with the chemical formula of CaO. The word lime originates with its earliest use as building mortar and has the sense of sticking or adhering."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Limestone_quarry.jpg/330px-Limestone_quarry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lime_(material)","wikidata":"Q250423"},{"title":"Online and offline","blocks":[{"text":"In computer technology and telecommunications, online indicates a state of connectivity, and offline indicates a disconnected state. In modern terminology, this usually refers to an Internet connection. More broadly, it could also refer to any piece of equipment or functional unit that is connected to a larger system. Being online means that the equipment or subsystem is connected, or that it is ready for use."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/O2_Wireless_Box_V.jpg/330px-O2_Wireless_Box_V.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Online_and_offline","wikidata":"Q10928179"},{"title":"Lime (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lime is a color that is a shade of yellow-green, so named because it is a representation of the color of the citrus fruit lime. It is the color that is in between the web color chartreuse and yellow on the color wheel. Alternate names for this color included yellow-green, lemon-lime, lime green, or bitter lime."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/AosaHGkyuai_%28cropped%29_3.jpg/330px-AosaHGkyuai_%28cropped%29_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lime_(color)","wikidata":"Q906936"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/The_lime_cycle.jpg/500px-The_lime_cycle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/The_lime_cycle.jpg/500px-The_lime_cycle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The lime cycle for high-calcium lime","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_lime_cycle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Lime_residue_thermal_water_Katlanovo_spa_1.jpg/500px-Lime_residue_thermal_water_Katlanovo_spa_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Lime_residue_thermal_water_Katlanovo_spa_1.jpg/1280px-Lime_residue_thermal_water_Katlanovo_spa_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Lime_residue_thermal_water_Katlanovo_spa_1.jpg/500px-Lime_residue_thermal_water_Katlanovo_spa_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lime formed to piping bringing thermal water to Katlanovo spa, North Macedonia.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALime_residue_thermal_water_Katlanovo_spa_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/The_Magdalen_Reading_-_Rogier_van_der_Weyden_%28cropped%2972.jpg/500px-The_Magdalen_Reading_-_Rogier_van_der_Weyden_%28cropped%2972.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/The_Magdalen_Reading_-_Rogier_van_der_Weyden_%28cropped%2972.jpg/500px-The_Magdalen_Reading_-_Rogier_van_der_Weyden_%28cropped%2972.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Magdalen_Reading_-_Rogier_van_der_Weyden_(cropped)72.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/16-09-17-WikiLovesCocktails-Zutaten-Img0144.jpg/500px-16-09-17-WikiLovesCocktails-Zutaten-Img0144.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/16-09-17-WikiLovesCocktails-Zutaten-Img0144.jpg/500px-16-09-17-WikiLovesCocktails-Zutaten-Img0144.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A16-09-17-WikiLovesCocktails-Zutaten-Img0144.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Bra